    desc: "Songye communities commission mankishi (plural bankishi), towering power figures built by sculptors and activated by ritual specialists: a carved standing body receives a bishimba charge of earth, minerals and substances in an abdominal cavity, while horns, feathers, beads, antelope hide and iron blades are lashed on as the figure accumulates protective office. Faces show vertical kaolin-white bands between heavy features; the surface darkens with repeated libations. Small personal nkishi guard individuals, community figures preside over villages — settling disputes, detecting sorcery, defending fertility — and are renewed rather than replaced. Their bristling assemblage aesthetic made them landmarks of Congolese art, displayed from the Met to Tervuren.",
